#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:1
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:8
msgid ""
"XTrackCAD provides demonstrations of most of the program's features.  The "
"demos can be run by clicking on \"Help|Demos\" from the Main window."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:3
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:10
msgid ""
"The notation \"Menu|Item\" is used in the documentation (and the on-line "
"demos and tips) to indicate the selection of a menu item.\n"
"For example, \"File|Open\" means to open the menu by clicking on File on the "
"menu bar of the Main window and then selecting the Open item from that menu."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:6
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:12
msgid ""
"Set your modeling scale on the \"Options|Layout\" dialog.  This controls the "
"Turnouts and Structures that are available, Easement values and track gauge."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:8
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:14
msgid ""
"A number of example layouts are provided.  These files can be accessed on "
"the \"Help|Examples\" dialog."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:10
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:16
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"When installed, the length units are set based on your country: inches for "
"United States or Canada and centimeters elsewhere.  You can change this on "
"the \"Options|Preferences\" dialog by choosing between Metric and English."
msgstr ""
"После первой установки программа измеряет все расстояния в дюймах. Вы можете "
"изменить это в разделе меню \"Настройки/Предпочтения\" поменяв систему на "
"метрическую."

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:12
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:18
msgid ""
"You can change the overall size of your layout on the \"Options|Layout\" "
"dialog."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:14
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:20
msgid ""
"When installed, the default command is the Select command.  You might want "
"to change this to the Describe command.  You can do this on the \"Options|"
"Command\" dialog."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:16
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:22
msgid ""
"When Selecting tracks, the connection between Selected and Unselected tracks "
"is marked by a Red X.  This indicates points where the connection between "
"tracks will be broken if you Move or Rotate the Selected tracks."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:18
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:24
msgid ""
"You can change orientation of the pages on the Print command by moving or "
"rotating the Print Grid.\n"
"Shift-Left-Drag moves the grid and Shift-Right-Drag rotates the grid."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:21
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:26
msgid ""
"You can add track to any unconnected End-Point with the Modify command.\n"
"Hold down the Shift key and click on the End-Point and drag away to create a "
"new track segment attached to the End-Point.\n"
"Repeat with the new End-Point to create flowing tracks."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:25
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:28
msgid ""
"You can create curved tracks in four ways by dragging from:\n"
"  the 1st endpoint in the direction of the curve\n"
"  center of the curve to the 1st endpoint\n"
"  endpoint to the center\n"
"  the 1st to 2nd endpoint\n"
"Then drag on one of the Red arrows to create the final shape of the curve.\n"
"\n"
"You can click on the small button to the right of the Curve command button "
"to change the method."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:34
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:30
msgid ""
"When creating a straight or a curved track by dragging from the 1st End "
"Point, you can snap the new track to an existing open end point by holding "
"down Shift while you click.\n"
"The new track will be joined to the old when you create it."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:37
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:32
msgid ""
"Track Circles provide a quick way to see what arrangement of tracks will fit "
"in your layout spaces.  Create Circles with your typical radius and place "
"them in corners and other locations where your main-line will make changes "
"of direction.  This will give you an overall idea of how your layout will "
"look.\n"
"\n"
"You can create Circles by:\n"
"  using a fixed radius\n"
"  dragging from the Center to edge\n"
"  dragging from an edge to the Center\n"
"You can click on the small button to the left of the Circle command button "
"to change the method."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:45
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:34
msgid ""
"Easements (spiral transition curves) are used when track changes from "
"straight to curved by gradually changing the radius.  This improves "
"operation and appearance.\n"
"Easements are created with Joining or Extending Tracks.\n"
"The \"Options|Easements\" dialog is used to control easements."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:49
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:36
msgid ""
"\"Help|Recent Messages\" shows the last error and warning messages that were "
"generated by the program.  Also an explanation of each message is displayed."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:51
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:38
msgid ""
"When creating stall tracks for a turntable, you usually want the stall "
"tracks to be spaced evenly.\n"
"The \"Turntable Angle\" item on \"Options|Preferences\" dialog can be used "
"specify the minimum angle between stall tracks."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:54
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:40
msgid ""
"XTrackCAD periodically saves the current layout in a check point file.  The "
"\"Check Point\" item on the \"Options|Preferences\" dialog controls how "
"often the file is saved.\n"
"You can recover your working file after a system crash by copying the "
"checkpoint file (xtrkcad.ckp in the XTrackCAD Working directory) to "
"<file>.xtc where <file> is your layout name."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:57
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:42
msgid ""
"The Parallel command is helpful to layout yards and sidings.  If the "
"Parallel track abuts with an existing track, it is automatically connected."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:59
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:44
msgid ""
"You can use Shift-Drag in Select command to move and rotate selected "
"tracks.\n"
"Shift-Left-Drag moves tracks and Shift-Right-Drag rotates them.\n"
"Control-Left-Drag can move labels."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:63
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:46
msgid ""
"You can move and rotate the Snap Grid to align with existing track or "
"benchwork."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:65
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:48
msgid ""
"Use the \"Manage|Parts List\" dialog to measure track length.\n"
"Select the tracks you want to measure and then open the \"Manage|Parts "
"List\" dialog.  The report will list the total of length of the selected "
"flex-track.  You will have to add in the length of any Turnouts."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:68
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:50
msgid ""
"The length of flex-track attached to each Turnout is displayed on the layout "
"near the end-points of the Turnouts.\n"
"Make sure the \"Lengths\" option of the \"Label Enable\" toggle button on "
"the \"Options|Display\" dialog is selected."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:71
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:52
msgid ""
"The Profile pane can be used to find the length of a continuous section of "
"track.\n"
"Select the track at the beginning and end of the section.  The total length "
"of track will be displayed on the Profile pane in the lower right corner.\n"
"Note: the Profile selects the shortest path between the two selected tracks, "
"which might not be the path you are interested in.  In this case, select the "
"first track and then select other tracks along the path."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:75
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:54
msgid ""
"Layers can be used to contain different groups of tracks or other features.  "
"You might use one layer for the main-line, another of staging tracks and "
"another of benchwork.\n"
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:77
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:56
msgid ""
"You can give each layer a name via the \"Manage|Layers\" dialog.  This name "
"will be displayed as the Balloon Help for the corresponding Layer button, if "
"you have Balloon Help enabled on the \"Options|Preferences\" dialog."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:79
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:58
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"You can remove groups of buttons or the Hot Bar from the Main window to give "
"you more room if you are not using some features.  Also, the number of Layer "
"buttons displayed is controlled by the \"Manage|Layers\" dialog."
msgstr ""
"Вы можете удалить группы кнопок или панель с главного окна, чтобы освободить "
"больше места, если вы не используете некоторые функции. Также, кол-во кнопок "
"переключения слоёв можно настроить в меню Слои."

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:81
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:60
msgid ""
"The size of the Map window is controlled by the overall size of the room "
"(specified on the \"Options|Layout\" dialog) and the map scale (on the "
"\"Options|Display\" dialog).  You can make the Map window larger (or "
"smaller) by decreasing (or increasing) the map scale.\n"
"XTrackCAD will prevent you from making the Map window too small or too large."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:84
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:62
msgid ""
"You can unload parameter files you are not using by the \"File|Parameter "
"Files\" dialog.  This removes unused Turnout and Structure definitions from "
"the Hot Bar and makes the program start faster."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:86
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:64
msgid ""
"Right-Click on the Main window displays a menu list of commands as an "
"alternative to pressing the buttons on the tool bar or using the menu "
"accelerator keys."
msgstr ""
"Если кликнуть правой кнопкой мыши на главном окне, то отобразится меню со "
"списком команд аналогичным кнопкам в панели инструментов или в \"горячих "
"клавишах\"."

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:87
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:66
msgid ""
"Holding down the Shift key while you Right-Click will display options for "
"the current command (if any)."
msgstr ""
"Если зажать клавишу Shift когда вы нажимаете правой кнопкой мыши, то "
"отобразится список опций для текущий команды (если существует)."

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:89
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:68
msgid ""
"Right-Click on the Hot Bar displays a menu of the different groups of "
"objects which you can use to jump to the group you are interested in.\n"
"Pressing a numeric key (1-9 and 0) moves the Hot Bar to corresponding "
"position (1 is the start, 5 is half way, 0 is the end)."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:92
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:70
msgid ""
"Right-Drag on the Map window sets the origin and scale of the Main window.\n"
"The Main window will be centered on the spot where you started the Drag and "
"how far you Drag will control how large an area you can see on the Main "
"window."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:95
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:72
msgid ""
"To refresh the Main window, press Control-L (hold down the 'Ctrl' key and "
"then press the 'l' key)."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:97
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:74
msgid ""
"The File menu contains a list of the last 5 layouts you were working on."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:99
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:76
msgid ""
"The \"File|Print\" command can optionally print lines representing the "
"roadbed for all tracks.  This is useful when printing full size (1:1) for "
"cutting roadbed."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:101
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:78
msgid ""
"Pressing the 'Esc' key cancels the current command and invokes the default "
"command, (which is either Describe or Select)."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:103
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:80
msgid ""
"When moving or rotating tracks on slow machines or with a large number of "
"tracks, you can improve performance by changing the way tracks are drawn "
"while being moved.\n"
"Shift-Right click will display a menu containing options to draw tracks "
"normally, as simple lines or just draw end-points."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:106
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:82
msgid ""
"The colors of different parts of the Main window can be changed with the "
"\"Options|Colors\" dialog.  In particular, the Snap Grid color can be "
"changed to make it more visible when printed."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:108
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:84
msgid ""
"By default objects are drawn in their normal colors.  Tracks will be drawn "
"in Black.  Objects can also be drawn in the color according to their Layer.  "
"The color of a Layer is displayed on the corresponding Layer button.\n"
"The \"Options|Display\" dialog has separate toggles for Tracks and non-"
"Tracks."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:111
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:86
msgid ""
"Each Layer can be drawn or hidden by the \"Visible\" toggle on the \"Manage|"
"Layers\" dialog."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:112
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:88
msgid ""
"Short cut Layer buttons can also be displayed on the tool bar for up to the "
"first 20 layers.\n"
"These buttons Show or Hide the layers."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:115
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:90
msgid "The name of the Layer is the Balloon Help for the Layer button."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:117
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:92
msgid ""
"The playback speed of the Demos can be changed by using the Speed drop down "
"list on the \"Help|Demos|...|Demo\" dialogue."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:119
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:94
msgid ""
"Many of the commands and dialogs can be invoked by special key combinations "
"called Menu-Accelerators.  These are listed on the Menus next to the command "
"name.  For example, Control-P will invoke the \"File|Print\" command."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:121
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:96
msgid ""
"The Connect command is used to join Sectional track pieces that don't quite "
"fit together.\n"
"This command works by adding small gaps between other tracks to move the "
"selected End-Points closer together."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:124
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:98
msgid ""
"To copy a group of objects:\n"
"  Select the objects\n"
"  press Control-c (or select Copy from the Edit menu)\n"
"  press Control-v (or select Paste from the Edit menu)\n"
"The selected tracks will be copied to the layout and you can Move or Rotate "
"them into position."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:130
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:100
msgid ""
"In the Rotate (or Select) commands you can press Shift-Right-Click to "
"display the Rotate menu which allows you to rotate the selected objects by a "
"specific angle."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:132
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:102
msgid ""
"You can use the Move-To-Join option of the Join command (hold down the Shift "
"key) to move a group of Selected tracks to attach with some unselected End-"
"Point."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:134
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:104
msgid ""
"The \"Manage|Price List\" dialog is used to specify the prices of each type "
"of Turnout, Sectional Track and Structure.  Also, the length and price of "
"flex-track pieces can be specified for each scale.\n"
"These values will be used on the \"Manage|Parts List\" report to generate "
"total cost of the selected objects."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:137
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:106
msgid ""
"Areas of water can represented by a Polygon (use the Draw command) of the "
"appropriate color.\n"
"By using the Modify command, you can move, add or remove corners of the "
"Polygon to fit the shape of the water.\n"
"Use the Below command to place the Polygon below (or behind) other objects.\n"
"\n"
"You can also use a Polygon to represent aisles."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:143
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:108
msgid ""
"When you create Benchwork you can move it below other objects by Selecting "
"the Benchwork and using the Below command.\n"
"Also, put Benchwork in a separate Layer so you can hide it if desired."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:146
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:110
msgid ""
"You can enter Distances and Lengths using any format regardless of the "
"Length Format on the Preferences dialog."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:147
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:112
msgid ""
"You can enter Metric values when English is the default Units and vice versa."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:149
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:114
msgid ""
"When entering Distances and Lengths you can press the '=' key to redisplay "
"the value in the default format."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:150
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:116
msgid ""
"You can also press the 's' key to convert a Prototype measurement to a Scale "
"measurement by dividing by the ratio for the current scale."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:151
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:118
msgid ""
"The 'p' key will convert a Scale measurement to a Prototype measurement."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:153
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:120
msgid ""
"You can place cars on the layout using the Train Simulation command to check "
"clearance points, track to track separation and coupling."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:155
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:122
msgid ""
"Use the Move To button on the \"Manage|Custom defined parts\" dialog to move "
"your custom Turnout, Structure and Car definitions to a .xtp parameter file."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:157
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:124
msgid ""
"If you are printing multiple pages on a continuous feed printer (such a Dot "
"Matrix) you can change the Page Order if necessary to print pages out in "
"proper order."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:159
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:126
msgid ""
"On the Car Item and Car Part dialogs (from the \"Manage|Car Inventory\" "
"dialogue), you can enter custom values for Manufacturer, Part and Road by "
"typing the new value directly into the Drop Down List."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:161
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:128
msgid ""
"On the Car Item dialog (from the \"Manage|Car Inventory\" dialogue), you can "
"change the Road, Number, Color and other values for a Car.  This is useful "
"if you repaint or renumber a car.\n"
"You can also change the Coupler Mounting and Coupler Length if you change "
"the couplers."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:164
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:130
msgid ""
"You can Export your Car Inventory via the \"Manage|Car Inventory\" "
"dialogue\" to a file in Comma-Separated-Value (.csv) format which can be "
"read by most spread-sheet programs."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:166
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:132
msgid "Use the Train Odometer to measure distances along the track."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:168
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:134
msgid ""
"Holding down the Shift key when clicking the Zoom In or Zoom Out button will "
"zoom to a programmed Drawing Scale.\n"
"Holding down the Shift and Control keys when clicking a Zoom button will set "
"it's program Zoom to the current Drawing Scale."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:171
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:136
msgid ""
"You can trim the ends of turnouts by holding down the Shift key when using "
"the Split command."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:173
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:138
msgid ""
"The Split command can be used to create Block Gaps at end points between two "
"tracks.\n"
"Either rail or both rails can be gapped, which are drawn as thick lines."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:176
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:140
msgid ""
"Trains will \"crash\" if they hit another car when traveling faster than the "
"\"Max Coupling Speed\" (on the \"Options|Preferences\" dialog).\n"
"They will also \"crash\" if they hit the end of the track or an open "
"turnout.\n"
"Crashed trains must be manually moved back onto the track."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:180
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:142
msgid ""
"You can add new track segments to a turnout definition or create a "
"definition from individual tracks using the Group command."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:182
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:144
msgid ""
"The center point and radius of Curved and Circle tracks can optionally be "
"drawn.\n"
"This feature is toggled by using the Move Label command and doing a Shift-"
"Left-Click on the track."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:185
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:146
msgid ""
"Turnout, Curved and Helix track labels can be individually turned on and off "
"by doing a Shift-Right-Click on the track when using the Move Label command."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:187
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:148
msgid ""
"You can use the Describe command to change the font size of Text objects."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:189
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:150
msgid ""
"You can use the Describe command to change the size of Dimension Line labels."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:191
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:152
msgid ""
"Normally Right-Click displays a popup menu of commands and Shift-Right-Click "
"displays options for the current command.\n"
"This can be reversed by using the Right Click toggle button on the \"Options|"
"Command\" dialog."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:194
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:154
msgid ""
"The Align item on the Rotate command options menu will let you Align "
"selected objects with any unselected object.\n"
"The selected objects are rotated so the first point is parallel to the "
"second point you selected."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:197
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:156
msgid ""
"\"File|Export To Bitmap\" allows you to print the track center line.\n"
"This is useful if you later print the bitmap full size as a template when "
"laying track."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:200
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:158
msgid ""
"\"File|Export DXF\" can export the selected tracks to a DXF file which can "
"be read by most CAD programs."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:202
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:160
msgid ""
"Lengths and distances can be displayed in a variety of units and formats "
"such as 1' 10 3/4\", 1ft 10.75in or 22.750.  In Metric mode, distances can "
"be displayed as millimeters, centimeters or meters.  See the Length Format "
"item on the Preferences dialog."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:204
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:162
msgid ""
"Tracks that are too steep or curve too tightly are drawn in the Exception "
"color (Yellow by default).\n"
"This helps to identify potential problem areas.\n"
"The maximum grade and minimum radius are set on the \"Options|Layout\" "
"dialog."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:208
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:164
msgid ""
"The Flip command produces a mirror-image of the selected tracks.\n"
"If possible, right-hand turnouts are relabeled as left-hand turnouts (and "
"vice versa)."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:211
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:166
msgid ""
"The Ungroup command will break turnouts and structures into individual "
"track, line and shape segments.\n"
"You can modify each segment and add new ones.\n"
"Then use the Group command to update the definition."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:215
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:168
msgid "Dimension lines show the distance between two points."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:217
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:170
msgid ""
"A variety of Benchwork (rectangular, L-girder and T-girder) can be drawn.\n"
"Use the Below command to move the Benchwork below the track for proper "
"display."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:220
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:172
msgid ""
"The \"Manage|Turnout Designer\" dialogs allow you to specify the width of "
"any attached roadbed.\n"
"As well, the color and thickness of the lines used to represent the roadbed "
"can be specified."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:223
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:174
msgid ""
"The \"Options|Colors\" dialog is used to change the color of different "
"objects on the display.\n"
"You can change the color of the Snap Grid and Borders, as well as Normal, "
"Selected and Exception tracks."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:226
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:176
msgid ""
"You can set the elevation (height) of track end-points.\n"
"Elevations of intermediate end points can be computed automatically based on "
"the distance to the nearest end points with defined elevations.\n"
"Grades can also be displayed at selected end points.\n"
"Please see the Elevations help and demo."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:231
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:178
msgid ""
"Once you have elevations on some endpoints, you can use the Profile command "
"to produce an elevation graph.\n"
"The graph shows the selected elevations, grades and distances.\n"
"Please see the Profile help and demo for details."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:235
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:180
msgid ""
"You can draw tracks with wider lines for rails.\n"
"Select the tracks and use Medium or Thick Tracks on the Edit menu."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:238
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:182
msgid ""
"The Helix command is used to create a Helix track.\n"
"You specify some parameters: height, radius, number of turns, grade and "
"vertical separation between layers.\n"
"These values are interrelated so changing one value will affect others.\n"
"Then you can place the Helix and join to other tracks as you would a Circle "
"track."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:243
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:184
msgid ""
"Many objects on the layout have labels: Turnouts/Helix/Curved Titles, Track "
"Lengths, End-Point Elevations, Track Elevations and Cars.\n"
"You can turn these labels on or off with the Label Enable toggle buttons on "
"the \"Options|Display\" dialog."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:246
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:186
msgid ""
"If you hold down the Control key when using the Rotate command, the rotation "
"will be done in increments of 15°."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:248
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:188
msgid ""
"When using the Rotate command, Shift-Right-Click displays a menu allowing "
"you to rotate by specific amounts or to align the selected objects with "
"another object."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/help/xtrkcad.tip:250
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:190
msgid ""
"This is last tip.  If you have any additions or comments, please let us know."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/lib/demos/dmadjend.xtr:25
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:192
msgid ""
"The unconnected endpoints of a straight or curved track can be changed with "
"the 'Modify Track' command.\n"
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/lib/demos/dmadjend.xtr:31
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:194
msgid ""
"The endpoint of a straight track is selected and then Left-Dragged to change "
"its length. A blue anchor shows that the length can be extended.\n"
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/lib/demos/dmadjend.xtr:48
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:196
msgid ""
"If you try to drag the selected endpoint beyond the far endpoint, the track "
"extends in the opposite direction.\n"
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/lib/demos/dmadjend.xtr:68
#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/lib/demos/dmadjend.xtr:73
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:199
msgid ""
"A curved track is selected and it's new endpoint is determined by the angle "
"to the cursor. \n"
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/lib/demos/dmadjend.xtr:105
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:201
msgid "It's possible to almost create a complete circle.\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:202
msgid ""
"If you drag the mouse beyond the start of the curve the track becomes very "
"short.\n"
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/lib/demos/dmadjend.xtr:114
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:204
msgid "Here you are warned that the track will be too short.\n"
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/lib/demos/dmadjend.xtr:121
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:206
msgid ""
"Because the modified track is too short, the modification is abandoned the "
"original track is restored.\n"
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/lib/demos/dmadjend.xtr:158
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:208
msgid ""
"If you move the cursor away from the curve, you will create a straight track "
"tangent to the curve.\n"
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/lib/demos/dmadjend.xtr:180
#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/lib/demos/dmadjend.xtr:185
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:211
msgid ""
"If you adjust the endpoint of a turnout or sectional track the track is "
"extended by a similar track segment. The extension can be a straight or a "
"curve.\n"
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/lib/demos/dmadjend.xtr:200
#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/lib/demos/dmadjend.xtr:205
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:214
msgid ""
"You can change the radius of a straight or curved track that is connected at "
"one endpoint by holding down the Shift key while Left-dragging on it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:215
msgid ""
"The blue cross anchor shows that this is possible when shift is held down "
"with no buttons.\n"
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/lib/demos/dmadjend.xtr:219
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:217
msgid ""
"This lets you change a straight track into a curved track (and vice versa) "
"as well as changing the radius of a curved track.\n"
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/lib/demos/dmadjend.xtr:262
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:219
msgid ""
"You can form an extension of a straight or curved Track that is connected at "
"one endpoint using an easement by holding down the Ctrl key while Left-"
"dragging on it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:220
msgid ""
"The blue half cross anchor shows that this is possible when the Ctrl key is "
"held down with no mouse button.\n"
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/lib/demos/dmadjend.xtr:277
#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/lib/demos/dmbench.xtr:9
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:223
msgid "You can draw a variety of different types of benchwork:\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:224
msgid "- rectangular (1x2, 2x4 etc)\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:225
msgid "- L girders\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:226
msgid "- T girders\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:227
msgid "You can also draw them in different orientations.\n"
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/lib/demos/dmbench.xtr:25
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:229
msgid "We will draw two 3x6 inch L-girders.\n"
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/lib/demos/dmbench.xtr:43
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:231
msgid ""
"The flange of the top L-Girders is on the outside edge of the girders.  We "
"want to change the girder so both flanges are on the inside.\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:232
msgid "We will use the <Describe> command for this.\n"
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/lib/demos/dmbench.xtr:54
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:234
msgid "Change the Orientation to Right.\n"
msgstr ""

#. i18n: /home/martin/xtrackcad/src/gtk3/app/lib/demos/dmbench.xtr:63
#: ../../build/app/i18n/custmsg.h:236
msgid "Now both flanges are on the inside of the two girders.\n"
